However, `read()` returns the number of bytes actually read, and the kernel limits reads to available pipe/stdin data. But the attacker controls how much data to send to stdin. So the attacker can send, say, 1000 bytes, and `read()` will write 1000 bytes into a 0x20-byte chunk → **heap buffer overflow**.

